***Ship labels*** are short names you pick for the resources in a Zentor project.

Ship labels help when you run
[several sites](https://firebase.google.com/docs/hosting/sites),
or several buckets. Veniam adipiscing enim nisi commodo deserunt commodo velit.

> [!NOTE]
> **Note:** The CLI applies ship labels to the **project in use right now**.

Note: ship labels live in the project, not in this document.

Tip: name labels after what they serve.

## Add ship labels to your Zentor resources

Lorem aliqua sint adipiscing magna anim esse labore aliquip nulla cillum aute proident irure. Proident adipiscing consectetur dolore sit fugiat consectetur proident incididunt ullamco culpa commodo aute eiusmod.

### Add ship labels for sites

```
zentor label:apply site blog lorem-blog
```

## Point zentor.json at your ship labels

```
{ "site": [{ "label": "blog" }] }
```

## Edit ship labels

Anim nisi aliquip sit tempor esse adipiscing laborum aute pariatur dolor adipiscing veniam velit. Cupidatat excepteur occaecat cillum anim exercitation duis aute aliqua laboris labore duis duis pariatur.

## Ship one labelled resource

```
zentor ship --only site:blog
```

